      "content_sha256": "52354a4e63cae0dce361f3c8cd23524001b8cc768f214e6882797370997eca93",
      "score": 100,
      "content": "# ILL224: See How Far One Agent Goes in Copilot Studio\n\n![Microsoft Frontier Tour 2027](img/banner-frontier-tour-27.png)\n\n[Microsoft Frontier Tour 2027](https://aitour.microsoft.com)\n\n### Session description\n\nBuild a Supplier Assurance Agent in Microsoft Copilot Studio that combines governed SharePoint knowledge, live SharePoint MCP operations, reusable skills, sandboxed Python, memory, evaluation, and workflow automation. Follow one realistic invoice review from submitted evidence to a human-review recommendation while preserving clear operational and financial guardrails.\n\n### Getting started\n\n#### In a guided session\n\n1. Open the Skillable environment provided by your instructor.\n2. Review the [lab overview](lab/README.md).\n3. Start with [Introduction and sign in](lab/instructions/00-Introduction.md).\n\n#### On your own\n\n1. Clone this repository.\n2. Review the [environment setup](environment/README.md) and provision the required services.\n3. Follow the [attendee instructions](instructions/README.md).\n\n### Learning outcomes\n\nBy the end of this session, you will be able to:\n\n- Build and ground a Copilot Studio agent with governed SharePoint content and live SharePoint MCP operations.\n- Create reusable agent skills that analyze an invoice with sandboxed Python and produce an auditable review artifact.\n- Validate and operationalize an agent with memory, evaluation, publishing, and a learner-built workflow.\n\n### Technologies used\n\n- Microsoft Copilot Studio\n- SharePoint Online and SharePoint MCP\n- Copilot Studio Workflows\n- Python\n- Skillable\n\n### Repository guides\n\n- [Attendee instructions](instructions/README.md)\n- [Environment and Skillable setup](environment/README.md)\n- [Generated lab package](package/README.md)\n- [Delivery resources](delivery-resources/README.md)\n\n### Continue your learning\n\n| Resource | What you'll get |\n| --- | --- |\n| [Microsoft Copilot Studio documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/microsoft-copilot-studio/) | Product concepts, authoring guidance, and administration documentation |\n| [Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com) | Official documentation and guided learning paths |\n| [Session recording](https://aka.ms/ft27/ill224/youtube) | Watch the ILL224 session recording |\n| [Frontier Tour 2027 Resource Center](https://aka.ms/FrontierTour27) | Additional Frontier Tour session repositories and materials |\n\n### Content owner\n\n[![April Dunnam](https://github.com/aprildunnam.png)](https://github.com/aprildunnam)\n\n**[April Dunnam](https://github.com/aprildunnam)**\n\n### Deliver this session\n\nPresenters and re-delivery partners can find the deck status, presenter notes, and delivery guidance in [delivery resources](delivery-resources/README.md).\n\n### Trademarks\n\nThis project may contain trademarks or logos for projects, products, or services. Authorized use of Microsoft trademarks or logos is subject to and must follow [Microsoft's Trademark & Brand Guidelines](https://www.microsoft.com/legal/intellectualproperty/trademarks/usage/general). Use of Microsoft trademarks or logos in modified versions of this project must not cause confusion or imply Microsoft sponsorship.\n\nAny use of third-party trademarks or logos is subject to those third parties' policies.\n\nAll supplier, invoice, contract, approval, quality, and policy content is fictional lab data.\n"
    },
