      "content": "# Delivery resources\n\nPresenter, re-delivery, and train-the-trainer materials for ILL224: See How Far One Agent Goes in Copilot Studio.\n\n## Core materials\n\n| Item | Link | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Delivery deck | Avail 10.12.26  | PowerPoint presentation |\n| Session recording | [ILL224 Recording](https://aka.ms/ft27/ill224/youtube) | Detailed delivery of ILL224 |\n| Attendee landing page | [Session README](../README.md) | Public starting point |\n| Lab instructions | [Attendee instructions](../instructions/README.md) | Guided and self-paced paths |\n| Presenter guidance | [Presenter guide](../presenter/README.md) | Timing, talk track, expected results, and recovery paths |\n\n## Delivery checklist\n\n- Review the session README and attendee instructions.\n- Add and open the public delivery deck.\n- Review the presenter guide and expected results.\n- Validate the environment, SharePoint provisioning, MCP operations, skills, evaluation, and workflow.\n- Confirm all learner package files match `package/checksums.sha256`.\n\n## Session preparation\n\nFollow the [environment setup guide](../environment/README.md), including its readiness validation and release gates. Use the [Copilot Studio Workflow setup](../environment/COPILOT_STUDIO_WORKFLOW_SETUP.md) to validate the learner-built three-node workflow without prebuilding it.\n\n## Run of show\n\nThe [presenter guide](../presenter/README.md#timing) contains the 60-minute timing, facilitation checkpoints, expected results, and recovery paths.\n\n## Demo reproducibility\n\nThe complete generated artifact set is documented in the [package README](../package/README.md). Rebuild it with the scripts in [`scripts/`](../scripts) and verify it with the package checksum manifest.\n\n## Support\n\nContent owner: [April Dunnam](https://github.com/aprildunnam)\n"
    },
    {
      "path": "package/README.md",
      "sha": null,
      "content_sha256": "8855258ba1196e327fa85edf1120b86eab2db225f5168fb0bf001121ecd63117",
      "score": 98,
      "content": "# ILL224 Package\n\nThis directory is generated by `../scripts`.\n\n## Contents\n\n- `SharePoint/core`: six authoritative DOCX/PDF knowledge files uploaded to the root of the `Contracts` library\n- `SharePoint/optional`: optional XLSX/PPTX content also uploaded to the `Contracts` library root\n- `SharePoint-Lists/seed-data`: CSV provisioning files for six SharePoint lists\n- `LearnerVM`: invoice input, the code-bearing skill ZIP, evaluation cases, and learner instructions\n- `checksums.sha256`: package integrity manifest\n\n## Skills\n\nThe completed agent uses two skills:\n\n| Skill | How it is supplied | Purpose |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `invoice-fact-check` | Learner creates it from blank during the lab | Gathers and structures cited facts without calculating or recommending |\n| `invoice-review-decision` | Uploaded from `LearnerVM/skills/invoice-review-decision.zip` | Runs packaged Python, applies policy, and creates the review PDF |\n\nOnly one ZIP is intentional. Packaging `invoice-fact-check` as a second upload would remove the create-from-blank skill-authoring exercise.\n\n## Build\n\nFrom `ILL224/scripts`, run:\n\n```bash\nnpm install\nnpm run build\n```\n\nThe build requires Python 3 with `openpyxl` and LibreOffice. All content is fictional lab data.\n"
    },
